Using the 21 % statutory federal income‑tax rate and the figures in the filing:

1. **Pre‑tax earnings for 2025**  
   \[
   \text{Pre‑tax earnings} = \text{Net income} + \text{Provision for income taxes}
   = \$112{,}010\text{ m} + \$20{,}719\text{ m}
   = \$132{,}729\text{ m}
   \]

2. **Expected tax at 21 %**  
   \[
   \text{Expected tax} = 0.21 \times \$132{,}729\text{ m}
   = \$27{,}873\text{ m}
   \]

So the computed expected federal income tax for Apple in fiscal year 2025, using the 21 % statutory rate, is **approximately $27.9 billion** (or **$27,873 million**).
